Title: "Rings and Fields"
Id: "832946c5-ae2c-47d4-b445-3ded9c71199c"


Text: "Equipping a set with both addition and multiplication gives rise to rings
       and fields. In a ring, addition forms an abelian group, multiplication
       forms a monoid, and multiplication distributes over addition."
Id: "7c74e436-b04f-4233-8161-ed9e8ffc13a7"


SectionTitle: "Rings"
Id: "0297b76e-dfa0-495e-a363-8f9f27d2ded3"


[\ring]
Declares: R ::= (X, +, *, 0, 1) is \set via X
specifies:
. + is \(associative, commutative)::binary.operation:on{X}
. * is \(associative)::binary.operation:on{X}
. 0 "in" X
. 1 "in" X
satisfies:
. [additive.identity]
  forAll: x "in" X
  then: x + 0 = x
. [additive.inverse]
  forAll: x "in" X
  then:
  . exists: y "in" X
    suchThat: x + y = 0
. [multiplicative.identity]
  forAll: x "in" X
  then:
  . x * 1 = x
  . 1 * x = x
. [distributive]
  forAll: a, b, c "in" X
  then:
  . a * (b + c) = (a * b) + (a * c)
  . (a + b) * c = (a * c) + (b * c)
Enables:
. capability: x_ "in" R :<->: x_ is \ring.element:of{R}
  written: "x_? \in R?"
Documented:
. called: "ring"
. description: "A ring $(R, +, *, 0, 1)$ consists of an abelian addition group,
                an associative multiplication with identity $1$, and two-sided
                distributivity."
Id: "5ca5fdca-692d-4f04-8420-aa01c909955d"


[\ring.element:of{R ::= (X, +, *, 0, 1)}]
Declares: x "in" X
when: R is \ring
Enables:
. capability: x_ [+] y_ :=> x_ |R.+| y_
  written: "x_? +? y_?"
. capability: x_ [*] y_ :=> x_ |R.*| y_
  written: "x_? *? y_?"
Documented:
. called: "element of ring $R?$"
. description: "An element of a ring $R$ is a member of its carrier set $X$."
Id: "7e51f2cf-8568-4819-af9d-80949b74d813"


Text: "A commutative ring is a ring whose multiplication operation is
       commutative."
Id: "64b4ac6a-9629-4aa7-89e2-9f0ea27e9a48"


[\(commutative)::ring]
Refines: R ::= (X, +, *, 0, 1)
satisfies:
. forAll: x, y "in" R
  then: x * y = y * x
Documented:
. adjective: "commutative"
. description: "A commutative ring is a ring in which $x * y = y * x$ for all
                elements."
Id: "2ddbe95a-149f-4596-8496-b214741d64a4"


SectionTitle: "Fields"
Id: "0c54d423-2239-4bcc-9398-cff3fa696e7c"


Text: "A field is a non-trivial commutative ring where every non-zero element
       possesses a multiplicative inverse."
Id: "93eece57-714d-474a-8c52-840bbb3f6621"


[\field]
Declares: F ::= (X, +, *, 0, 1) is \(commutative)::ring via (X, +, *, 0, 1)
satisfies:
. 0 != 1
. forAll: x "in" F
  where: x != 0
  then:
  . exists: y "in" F
    suchThat: x * y = 1
Enables:
. capability: x_ "in" F :<->: x_ is \field.element:of{F}
  written: "x_? \in F?"
Documented:
. called: "field"
. description: "A field is a commutative ring $(F, +, *, 0, 1)$ with $0 \neq 1$
                in which every non-zero element has a multiplicative inverse."
Id: "53a76a9b-97d9-4c4d-b6c6-cc00983cfcb2"


[\field.element:of{F ::= (X, +, *, 0, 1)}]
Declares: x is \ring.element:of{F}
when: F is \field
Documented:
. called: "element of field $F?$"
. description: "An element of a field $F$ is an element of its underlying ring."
Id: "1961828f-5a83-4c78-b8c9-a91c2e512d50"


SectionTitle: "Ideals, Quotients, and Characteristic"
Id: "ca7d140b-b005-46b1-b844-511a2293e65d"


[\ideal:of{R ::= (X, +, *, 0, 1)}]
Declares: I \:subset:/ X
when: R is \ring
satisfies:
. 0 "in" I
. forAll: x, y "in" I
  then: x + y "in" I
. forAll: x "in" I
  then:
  . exists: y "in" I
    suchThat: x + y = 0
. forAll: r "in" R
  then:
  . forAll: i "in" I
    then:
    . r * i "in" I
    . i * r "in" I
Documented:
. called: "ideal of $R?$"
. description: "An ideal is an additive subgroup closed under multiplication by
                arbitrary ring elements."
Id: "999d97fa-3609-4900-a19d-ab1f3345ca54"


[\(zero.divisor)::ring.element:of{R ::= (X, +, *, 0, 1)}]
Refines: a
when: R is \(commutative)::ring
satisfies:
. a != 0
. exists: b "in" R
  suchThat:
  . b != 0
  . a * b = 0
Documented:
. adjective: "zero divisor"
Id: "cff0d878-33b9-4552-93c2-cee960162e9e"


[\integral.domain]
Declares: D ::= (X, +, *, 0, 1) is \(commutative)::ring via (X, +, *, 0, 1)
satisfies:
. 0 != 1
. forAll: a, b "in" D
  then:
  . if: a * b = 0
    then:
    . anyOf:
      . a = 0
      . b = 0
Documented:
. called: "integral domain"
. description: "A nontrivial commutative ring without zero divisors."
Id: "be91bf4c-366f-430f-bff8-6f9c7225736d"


TextDefinition: "The characteristic of a ring with identity is the least
                 positive integer $n$ such that $n\cdot1=0$, if such an integer
                 exists, and is $0$ otherwise. The characteristic of an integral
                 domain is either $0$ or prime. Consequently every field
                 contains a canonical copy of either $\mathbb{Q}$ or a finite
                 prime field $\mathbb{F}_p$."
Id: "e5fe50b7-6f61-4ad4-85e8-0fec0260b2cf"


TextTheorem: "For a commutative ring $R$, the quotient $R/I$ is an integral
              domain exactly when $I$ is prime, and it is a field exactly when
              $I$ is maximal. These correspondences turn questions about ideals
              into structural questions about quotient rings."
Id: "81f097c0-c0ee-4819-8304-7f13856e2551"
